{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966781,"nonce":"+14I6GEkiC+KqMICXE9gv7ooUj8=","title":"An FSM transition writing several context fields notified on each write; a Stateful refresh","message":"Symptom: a bound `cn.Button` label / `cn.Kbd` text stayed stale after\nclicking, then caught up on the *next* interaction. Whichever context\nfield the transition wrote FIRST appeared to work; everything written\nafter it lagged by one interaction.\n\n**Cause.** `refresh_stateful` does not queue a marker — it re-runs the\nStateful's callback and queues the element it BUILT. `on Idle.Busy`\nwrites `ctx.busy` then `ctx.caption`. The `busy` write notified\nimmediately, so the root Stateful rebuilt the whole view with `caption`\nstill at its old value. The `caption` write then queued its own\nrebuild, which the drain dropped as \"node no longer exists\" — the first\nrebuild had already replaced those nodes.\n\n**Fix.** `blinc_core::reactive::batch_stateful_deps` collects signal ids\nfor the duration of an FSM transition and fires one notification after\nthe last write, so the rebuild is built from the finished state.\nRe-entrant; only the outermost call flushes. Applied in\n`fsm::dispatch_default`.\n\nNot specific to any widget. Any transition writing more than one\ncontext field had it.\n\n**Diagnostic method that worked**, after several wrong theories: a\n`queued structural rebuild` trace at the queue site plus the existing\n`Processing N pending subtree rebuilds` drain log, then one real click.\nThe queue order and the \"no longer exists\" drops named the cause\ndirectly. Headless tests kept passing because they either wrote one\nfield or called `dispatch_default` after all writes.\n\nTwo traps met on the way:\n- `BlincContextState::init` without a callback leaves\n  `set_stateful_deps_notifier` uninstalled, so a bare `Signal::set`\n  reaches no Stateful and a headless reactivity test measures nothing.\n  The windowed runner now installs it unconditionally rather than only\n  when it is first to initialise the context state.\n- Tests in one binary share the process-global signal / FSM registries\n  by name. Give each its own names AND a file-local mutex, or they pass\n  alone and fail in a parallel run.\n\nSee also gotcha stale subtree rebuild across builds (the other\n\"queued rebuild meets a tree that moved on\" bug),\nfeedback signal subtree not full tree.","files":null}]}